.TH "MAW-TROUBLESHOOTING" "7" "" "maw 0.2.3" "maw manual"
.SH NAME
maw-troubleshooting \- doctor, logs, and where to look
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
When something on the machine doesn't work, start with \fBmaw doctor\fR. For anything maw manages, the commands below show where it stands.
.SH "DOCTOR"
.PP
.EX
maw doctor
.EE
.PP
\fBstatus\fR compares your machine with your repo; \fBdoctor\fR looks for problems that break a desktop quietly, which nothing in your repo would show:
.PP
.EX
warn no shared session bus
     declare a core dbus user service: `maw help modules`, under lib.service
warn /etc/pam.d/greetd doesn't unlock the keyring
     add `-auth optional pam_gnome_keyring.so` and `-session optional pam_gnome_keyring.so auto_start`
.EE
.PP
It checks for:
.IP \(bu 2
a session bus the keyring, apps, and user services share
.IP \(bu 2
greetd starting your session through \fBdbus-run-session\fR, which gives it a private bus
.IP \(bu 2
greetd without a \fBvt\fR
.IP \(bu 2
a keyring your login doesn't unlock
.IP \(bu 2
Electron apps without the hint to use Wayland
.IP \(bu 2
user services without \fBturnstiled\fR
.IP \(bu 2
the bin dirs of declared cargo, go, uv, npm, and flatpak programs missing from \fBPATH\fR
.PP
With nothing to report, it prints \fBall good\fR.
.SH "WHERE TO LOOK"
.IP \(bu 2
\fBA file isn't what you declared\fR: \fBmaw status\fR lists everything out of sync, and \fBmaw diff\fR shows each file's difference; a file edited in place is drift (\fBmaw help drift\fR).
.IP \(bu 2
\fBA service isn't running\fR: \fBmaw sv status <name>\fR, then \fBmaw sv log <name>\fR; see logs (\fBmaw help logs\fR).
.IP \(bu 2
\fBA module doesn't evaluate\fR: \fBmaw build\fR names the file and line; \fBmaw edit <name>\fR reopens it after an error.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBBefore a risky change\fR: \fBmaw activate --dry-run\fR lists every step without taking any.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBAfter a bad change\fR: \fBmaw rollback\fR returns files and packages to the last generation; see rolling back (\fBmaw help rolling back\fR).
.PP
Next: chapter 15, reference (\fBmaw help 15\fR).
